From: HeavyGee <gc@lockhouse.systems>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 17:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(soup): render NativeAppPromoSheet, and drop its dead sibling import

`verify-sessionlist-bindings` (a HARD gate in the remat's verify stage) fails
the compose with:

  web/src/router.tsx: imports NativeAppPromoSheet but never renders
  <NativeAppPromoSheet /> — entry point unreachable

PROVENANCE: upstream parent f288d8511 and origin/main both render
`<NativeAppPromoSheet enabled={isSessionsIndex} />` at router.tsx:392. The fork
parent had no render site, so the merge took the fork side of that region and
kept only the import. An upstream addition dropped — the one direction this
absorb is never allowed to resolve that way.

WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN A MISSING MODAL: `markPromoFirstSeen()` is called from
exactly one place, this sheet, and `shouldShowPromoModal` requires
`state.firstSeenAt !== undefined`. The component that ARMS the state machine is
the one gated on it, so unmounted it disarms itself permanently — the modal
could never appear even if something else mounted it.

WHY A HEAL. The render site sits in a conflict-free region of router.tsx, so git
treats it as context, rerere never replays it, and a hand fix is discarded by
the next recompose. Proven twice on 2026-11-24: this exact fix was committed to
driver/integration-wip, the compose recomposed, and the commit went dangling
(held only by tag rescue/2026-11-24-promo-sheet) while the gate demanding it —
landed on MAIN, where it persists — kept failing. The gate survived and its fix
did not, which is the whole argument for heals.

Also drops `NativeAppPromoButton` from SessionHeader.tsx: an unused import,
verified NOT a third instance of the same bug before deleting — that button IS
rendered, from router.tsx.
