    fix(web): render the native-app promo sheet, dropped as an upstream addition
    
    Generalising yesterday's Garden/XR chip fix into a tree-wide sweep for
    imported-but-unrendered components found a SECOND instance of the same class.
    That is the point of the sweep: one occurrence is a bug, two is a defect class,
    and the class is what the gate now covers.
    
    `NativeAppPromoSheet` (web/src/components/NativeAppPromo.tsx:226, props
    `{ enabled: boolean }`) was imported at web/src/router.tsx:2 and rendered
    nowhere.
    
    PROVENANCE — an upstream addition dropped, which is the one direction this
    absorb is not allowed to resolve that way. Upstream parent f288d8511 and
    current origin/main BOTH render `<NativeAppPromoSheet enabled={isSessionsIndex} />`
    at router.tsx:392. Fork parent 360c9d58d has no render site at all. So the
    merge took the fork side of that region and kept only the import. Restored at
    our line 1375, inside the same SessionsPage function where `isSessionsIndex`
    is already defined (line 330), so the prop means what upstream means by it.
    
    THE CONSEQUENCE IS WORSE THAN A MISSING MODAL, and is why this is not simply a
    cosmetic restore. `markPromoFirstSeen()` is called from exactly one place —
    this sheet, line 235 — and `shouldShowPromoModal` requires
    `state.firstSeenAt !== undefined`. The component that ARMS the state machine
    is the one gated on it. Unmounted, it disarms itself permanently: the modal
    could never have appeared on the promoted tip even if something else had
    mounted it. A reader checking only "is the promo feature wired?" would find a
    complete-looking state machine and no way to reach it.
    
    WHY NOTHING CAUGHT IT. The same structural blindness as the chip: typecheck is
    content with an unused import, there is no router test harness, and zero tests
    anywhere reference the component (grep NativeAppPromoSheet across
    web/src/**/*.test.tsx: no hits). Git treated the region as CONTEXT, not
    conflict, so no amount of careful conflict resolution would have surfaced it.
    
    THE GATE, extended rather than re-invented.
    verify-sessionlist-bindings.mjs already runs from the build and already failed
    closed on an unrendered entry point; `ENTRY_POINT_COMPONENTS` now carries both
    components. Its remediation hint was hardcoded to the chip's home
    (`toolbarExtras`), which would have sent the next reader to the wrong file for
    this component — it is now per-component and names upstream's own line.
    Positive control, both directions: deleting the render makes it exit 1 with
    "imports NativeAppPromoSheet but never renders <NativeAppPromoSheet /> —
    entry point unreachable / Render it in the SessionsPage shell, as upstream
    does at router.tsx:392", and restoring it returns OK (31 files).
    
    ALSO, one genuinely dead import removed: SessionHeader.tsx imported
    `NativeAppPromoButton` and never used it. Verified it is not a third instance
    of the same bug before deleting — the button IS rendered, at router.tsx:1284.
    Deleting a live binding to quiet a gate would have been the opposite of this fix.
    
    web 5556 passed / 1 expected fail / 0 failed (498 files, exit 0; floor 5557
    unchanged). typecheck:web exit 0. verify-sessionlist-bindings OK.
    
    via [HAPI](https://hapi.run)
    
    Co-Authored-By: HAPI <noreply@hapi.run>

